# LF everywhere, Windows checkouts included. The Windows release is built on a GitHub runner whose
# git has `core.autocrlf=true`: without this every multi-line string compiled into the app — the
# shell scripts it feeds to containers, `include_str!` files, bundled JS — shipped with `\r\n`, and
# `sh` read `then\r` as a command (Contenedores › Archivos listed nothing on Windows).
* text=auto eol=lf
